        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഇരുട്ട്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇരുട്ട് — iruṭṭŭ — \"darkness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കറന്റ് പോയി, വീട് മുഴുവൻ ഇരുട്ടിലായി. kaṟanṟŭ pōyi, vīṭŭ muḻuvan iruṭṭilāyi. The power went and the whole house was in darkness."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In the dark is ഇരുട്ടിൽ. The adjective ഇരുണ്ട, dark, has the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇരുട്ട് (iruṭṭŭ) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2552 lists Malayalam iruṭṭu, \"darkness\", with iruḷ and the verb for growing dark."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
