        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: നിശ്ശബ്ദത",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നിശ്ശബ്ദത — niśśabdata — \"silence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അറിയിപ്പ് കേട്ടപ്പോൾ ക്ലാസിൽ നിശ്ശബ്ദത പരന്നു. aṟiyippŭ kēṭṭappōḷ klāsil niśśabdata parannu. When they heard the notice, silence spread through the class."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The adjective is നിശ്ശബ്ദമായ, silent; the -ത ending makes the noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നിശ്ശബ്ദത (niśśabdata) is built from Sanskrit niḥśabda, \"noiseless, silent\" (Monier-Williams), with -ത, the ending that makes a noun of a state. The visarga of niḥ- becomes a second ശ before ശബ്ദം (śabdaṁ), so the word is written with ശ്ശ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
